# Nanalu Boutique — environment variables (template)
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#     cp .env.example .env.local
# `.env.local` is gitignored — real secrets NEVER get committed. This template
# is the committed contract: every variable the app reads should be listed here
# (with a safe placeholder), so a fresh clone knows what to set.
#
# DATABASE_URL is needed now (Phase 1). The rest stay commented out as
# placeholders until the code that reads them lands (see PLAN.md).

# — Database: PostgreSQL via Prisma —
# Default points at the local docker-compose `db` service (user/pass/db all
# "nanalu"). `docker compose up -d`, copy this to .env.local, and it just works.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://nanalu:nanalu@localhost:5432/nanalu?schema=public"

# — Image storage: Cloudinary (swappable later via an image-access layer) —
# The cloud name is PUBLIC — it appears in every delivered image URL — so it
# carries the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and is read by the image helper (src/lib/image.ts)
# in the browser too. Needed now (#31). "demo" is Cloudinary's public sandbox cloud,
# a safe placeholder until we create the real account.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME="demo"
# The API key/secret are for UPLOADS only (admin, Phase 8) — server-only, never
# NEXT_PUBLIC_. Still placeholders until that code lands.
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=""
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=""

# — Payments: Stripe (card data goes browser → Stripe; we store only tokens) —
# Publishable key is exposed to the browser, hence the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# The secret key is server-only — never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# — Auth (vetted provider, TBD — never hand-rolled) —
# AUTH_SECRET=""
